  "startingRecipe": "Continue original presentation stop323 from jungle-presentation. Checked code bytes at main00dc,0680,047c. Run00dc stop324 and capture CPU+DS+incoming driver color;run0680 stop325 and capture independent returned joystick AL0 with CPU+DS;run047c stop326 and capture CPU+DS+outgoing color. No input,register,memory write or restore added. All keys released,no schedules/breakpoints at326. Conditional initialization reuses original entry230 and platform-after246 from jungle-hazards,with a virtual descriptor factory replaying original loader/initializer order.",
  "environmentContract": "Conditional loader starts from original entry BEFORE230,with initial campaign options checked there. It allocates its own virtual descriptors; original AFTER246 supplies expected outputs only. Compare all declared entity/map/pickup/edge arrays,actor scalar fields,palette,RNG and resource descriptor geometry/frame. Normalize only sprite-pointer fields in the explicitly enumerated animation tuples to asset IDs. Whole frame starts once from BEFORE324,consumes recorded joystick/color BEFORE outputs,then carries all game state through invalidation,input,ground,camera,hazards,rider,motion and presentation. Independent replay starts from original executable static data and original archives,zero BSS,authored campaign parameters,virtual descriptors and its own clock provider;it carries all game state with no expected state/heap/timer insertion. Each translated synchronous segment has a logical completion timestamp;publication,next input and outgoing sound are held until the independently advanced driver clock reaches it. Retraces use a separate provider. Internal phase states during a queued logical wait are not original checkpoints.",
  "comparisonRules": "Conditional loader compares the specified semantic fields/arrays exactly;it does not compare DOS allocator state,freed resources,archive handles,stack or device fields. Whole-frame comparison is exact entire64K DS except9df2..9e71 helper stack and2225..2228 IRQ8 counter;no game globals,RNG,descriptor or dirty-list exclusions. Outgoing color exact. Independent replay requires20 exact snapshots/full-DS hashes/presentation-payload hashes,824 consumed input bytes,6405 clock events and875 presentations,then exact final state and outcome. Its expected values are authored port regression outputs,not original gameplay captures.",
  "limitations": [
    "The EGA striped wipe/reveal translates the five interlaced row groups and five retraces per group. Wipe masks explicitly preserve incoming renderer pixels;the incoming screen is never a simulation input. Transition pixel/timing comparison against the original remains unverified.",
    "Original whole-frame case is neutral at the initial viewport and has no wait/audio consumption. It does not prove original scrolling,whole-loop timing,fish boarding,other hazards or full-level parity.",
    "Independent replay reaches scroll960 through fish travel and ends in failure. Treasure success and other variants/difficulties still need acceptance scenarios.",
    "Browser acceptance exercises real resource loading,input,rendering,life loss,campaign return and direct retry;no full original campaign replay or audio parity claim."
  ],
